=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 419
title: A Makefile that builds instead of testing is still production, but no longer holds a weakened Python assertion at warn
origin: successor of runner_build_makefile_neg with the same inputs, re-pinned by the #419 ruling
origin2: (issuecomment-6170353038: Q1 (b), Q5 (b), rule 2). Content still decides the role: the recipe
origin3: runs no test runner, so the file stays production and the exact count forbids
origin4: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED. A Python test refuses its opaque-change evidence for ASSERT_WEAKENED.
=== before: Makefile ===
libfast.so: fast.c
	$(CC) -O2 -shared -o libfast.so fast.c
=== after: Makefile ===
libfast.so: fast.c
	$(CC) -O3 -shared -fPIC -o libfast.so fast.c
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) > 0
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "ASSERT_WEAKENED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["OPAQUE_PROD_CHANGE_NOT_EVIDENCE"]}]
